load\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"2d7686d82084977163ee2f30e2d65ee2b52511a816016628dc18d73482a99ea4","event_uuid":"b100d60f-6d2d-4b33-bce8-5c0596746b60","position":{"commit_sha":"4ded879350469674c9e9a264329af2a9f1822563","position":"1787347466341009331-b100d60f-6d2d-4b33-bce8-5c0596746b60"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"504d4024e656691c5a23cb7d43d77c5896ddae843926035b5e68d87f246c63b1","event_uuid":"75f02b1b-017a-4489-8f74-a780bff3f5a8","position":{"commit_sha":"f2ab4d77172572562d7ef855927934e3e9d60790","position":"1787351490195750001-75f02b1b-017a-4489-8f74-a780bff3f5a8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a547db25e3ec37695223c4e976b6b3b3714bdfa11a1e8e96c216a33cd1df5d97","event_uuid":"c7ceeac5-8992-433f-81a4-7bed49fbcd71","position":{"commit_sha":"a55a9797fa900cce3b0256a38b6a89af6598fe14","position":"1787352155080254001-c7ceeac5-8992-433f-81a4-7bed49fbcd71"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"887ed5eea2ff79d5bd97917037097111374a7c628645a8d6b0baf202f3ed80df","event_uuid":"75dc5222-e6ca-466a-9d66-7d1481333a26","position":{"commit_sha":"36813f1171cc1cc399ba37ca4cf2302c7acdcde4","position":"1787352160273884001-75dc5222-e6ca-466a-9d66-7d1481333a26"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787345850922432001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"27ae88a6-9893-474b-8684-a7f178edfc16","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"a8ea-be28-2394-4f0c"},{"link_uuid":"b100d60f-6d2d-4b33-bce8-5c0596746b60","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ffb4-74e3-dc3c-4b0f"}],"description":"# Split outbound_differ.py below the module-size cap (prerequisite for S3/S6)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\n`outbound_differ.py` sits at **799/800 LOC** — the hard module-size cap enforced by the\nCI-only gate in `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` against `.github/module-size-limit.txt`\n(=800; strict `>`). S2 (438a) drove it to 799 via `repo_root` threading. S3 (`a8ea`,\nconfig-driven type mapping) and S6 (`d458`) both MUST add code here — S3 needs a `rebar-type:`\nstamp invocation site (mirroring the `rebar-status:` stamp invoked ~line 763) and per-project\ntype-skip threading through `compute_outbound_mutations` (~line 374, where `EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES`\nis loaded and passed to `_compute_outbound_select_absent_gets`). Any addition breaches 800 and\nfails CI `Verified`. This is a pure prerequisite refactor — no behaviour change.\n\n## Approach\n\nExtract along an EXISTING call-graph seam (per AGENTS.md module-size policy — never\nmechanically, never a <100-LOC fragment). The two per-ticket mutation builders,\n`_compute_outbound_create_mutation` (lines 525–632, ~108 LOC) and\n`_compute_outbound_update_mutation` (lines 633–799, ~167 LOC), form a natural cluster: both are\ncalled ONLY by the `compute_outbound_mutations` orchestrator and both build a single\n`OutboundMutation` from a local/Jira ticket pair. Move the pair into a new sibling module\n`outbound_mutation_builders.py`. `compute_outbound_mutations` imports them back. Shared helpers\nthey use (`OutboundMutation`, `_load_config`, `_effective_status_map_for`, the mapper imports,\n`_best_effort`, `_is_retired`) either move with the cluster or are imported by the new module\nfrom `outbound_differ` / their existing homes — the implementer resolves the exact import edges\nso both modules type-check and no cycle forms. Result: `outbound_differ.py` ≈ 525 LOC, new\nmodule ≈ 290 LOC — both comfortably in the 200–500 target band.\n\nPublic API is unchanged: `compute_outbound_mutations`, `OutboundDiffConfig`, `OutboundMutation`\nkeep their import paths (re-export the mutation builders from `outbound_differ` if any test\nimports them by their private name). `tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` mirrors the gate\nand must stay green.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py` — remove the two builder functions;\n  import them from the new module; keep the orchestrator + dataclasses + top helpers.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_mutation_builders.py` (new) — the extracted\n  `_compute_outbound_create_mutation` + `_compute_outbound_update_mutation` cluster.\n\n## Testing\n\nPure behaviour-preserving refactor — the EXISTING outbound-differ suite is the oracle, run\nUNCHANGED (no new behavioural test is authored; a refactor that needs a new behavioural test\nwas not behaviour-preserving). The module-size contract test is the structural oracle.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `outbound_differ.py` and `outbound_mutation_builders.py` are EACH < 800 LOC and within the\n  200–500 target band — verified by\n  `find src/rebar -name '*.py' | grep -v __pycache__ | xargs wc -l | awk '$1>800'` (empty) and\n  by `tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` passing.\n- [x] The reconciler outbound suite passes GREEN unchanged — verified by\n  `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/ -k outbound` (no observable-behaviour change).\n- [x] The extraction is a single existing call-graph seam (the two `compute_outbound_mutations`\n  builders); no symbol's public import path changed (private-name importers get a re-export).\n\nTest tier: **refactor** — no new behaviour; the existing suite + the module-size contract are\nthe full oracle. Discovered during S3 (`a8ea`) plan-review round 1.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py","reason":"remove the two mutation-builder functions; import them from the new module"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_mutation_builders.py","reason":"new module holding the extracted create+update mutation builders"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","3d7a-7795-efde-4df7"],["relates_to","ffb4-74e3-dc3c-4b0f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","parent_status_uuid":"c7ceeac5-8992-433f-81a4-7bed49fbcd71","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f1bc-75f6-ed8c-472f","ticket_type":"task","title":"Split outbound_differ.py below module-size cap (prerequisite for S3/S6)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ffd9ec21-10fb-4c6c-b3b2-fa8c6ea0cd7c","27ae88a6-9893-474b-8684-a7f178edfc16","c2e17acf-2865-49e9-9eb6-5492dbc83fd1","9ef487bd-d7bb-4d1c-8537-af5ecb81205a","858d5ff3-73a6-44f6-a823-54543848f74e","6e58b5dd-dcab-4e35-be9c-d3d7ef46bc17","94c3f363-c239-4979-8c52-475060132b33","b100d60f-6d2d-4b33-bce8-5c0596746b60","75f02b1b-017a-4489-8f74-a780bff3f5a8","c7ceeac5-8992-433f-81a4-7bed49fbcd71","75dc5222-e6ca-466a-9d66-7d1481333a26"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787354432609029001,"uuid":"02af3a59-d66e-48e0-8096-48787d47ff24"}